From 0ed07eae099cfda1ad023408ff4545a34e052757 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrik Eriksson <patrik.m.eriksson@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:18:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] cdng, rec: APERTAR_DNG_DONTNEED chooses when a DNG's
 pages leave the page cache; dropped_copy_slot in the stats line

Why: the writer calls posix_fadvise(POSIX_FADV_DONTNEED) right after writing a DNG. In Linux 6.12
(mm/fadvise.c) that call starts the file's writeback and then, because the pages are still dirty
or in flight, fails to invalidate them and runs lru_add_drain_all(): work queued on every CPU and
waited for, 25 to 50 times a second, freeing nothing. The per-frame sync_file_range that follows
starts a writeback the DONTNEED already started. The kb's research (working/dng-chain, R3, R5,
R6) found this and showed the A1-versus-A2 reading of 2026-10-30 rests on it. cinepi-raw makes
no such call. The stop-time stats printed dropped_copy_slot only when it was above zero, so a
clean take could not show the counter was watched.

What: APERTAR_DNG_DONTNEED=writer (default, unchanged), sync (the sync thread drops a file's pages
after its fsync, when they are clean and the call is cheap) or off. With sync and the sync thread
disabled, Core logs one line. dropped_copy_slot is now a field of the "recording stats" line.

Tested: the encoder and the whole CameraController.cpp syntax-check (libcamera block on, no new
errors); tools/dng_payload_write_test.sh passes. Not run on the Pi: the A/B is A0 against
APERTAR_DNG_DONTNEED=sync against =off, 10 minutes each, with Cached from /proc/meminfo sampled
and bpftrace counting lru_add_drain_all.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NEFc1zNNwfkFFgzHEzb7wV
